 "summary": "Partly falsified: one of the card's three claims is an objectui defect, and the PR fixes that one and pins the other two. (1) TOAST: not reproduced in objectui. Through the real ObjectView, action:bar, action:button, ActionRunner, console runtime and ConsoleToaster (sonner unmocked), Invite User with the served sys_user shape renders the declared successMessage 'Invitation sent' in the toaster DOM after Confirm. Zone 2 hypothesis 1 (the list-toolbar path drops successMessage) is refuted. No real-browser reading exists, so why the reporter's browser saw no toast is not measured. (2) SUBTITLE: objectui already subtitles a parameter dialog with a declared description (served ban_user shape). invite_user and approval_approve declare none, so the generic line is right for them; their descriptions are objectstack metadata. (3) NESTED ANCHOR: reproduced. The Invitations list's first column is email, and EmailCellRenderer drew its mailto anchor and copy button inside the primary-field record anchor. Fixed in packages/plugin-grid: a link cell draws the self-linking types (email, url, phone, file, video, audio) with their text face (linkCellRenderer in cellRendererResolution.ts), and renders its children with the host's recordHref and openRecord withheld, so a reference prints its name. A census over every listCellRendererTypes() type in a link column found the file family, which then joined the set; the census now holds the class. The PR opens with 'Fixes #11817' as dispatched: objectui's share of every claim is either fixed or measured not to be an objectui defect, and the metadata halves go to objectstack (out_of_scope_findings).",
 "tests": "All runs at the worktree root through os-verify-lock (slot os-dev-11817). UNION at 484906c (the head, after merging main 04c8f56): pnpm exec vitest run --maxWorkers=2 packages/plugin-grid/ plus app-shell ObjectView.inviteFeedback-11817, ObjectView.emptyStateMatchesPage-11687, ActionParamDialog and useConsoleActionRuntime.paramDialogTitle gave 'Test Files 193 passed (193)', 'Tests 1816 passed (1816)', UNION_EXIT=0, 'VERDICT command-exit 0'. Earlier at 27653b8: plugin-grid package plus the new app-shell pin gave 'Test Files 190 passed (190)', 'Tests 1753 passed (1753)'. ABLATION, through /home/user/objectstack/scripts/ablation-replace.mjs on committed state, src-aliased so there is no dist leg. Leg 1 at 1edf68a disabled the text-face substitution (anchor x1 to x0, blob aeb945d to d331049): 7 failed and 10 passed (the email, url, phone and file first columns, the link:true email column, the census, the Invitations end-to-end case), then 'ok restored: blob == HEAD (aeb945d86253) and git diff HEAD is empty'. Leg 2 at 27653b8 removed the RelatedRecordActionsProvider override: the first attempt was a NO-OP, refused by the tool ('the replacement count moved 2 -> 2'), so nothing landed. The re-run with unique replacement '{children /* ablation-11817 */}' (x0 to x1, blob 63df3a1 to c868190) gave 2 failed and 8 passed (the reference-in-link-column case and the census), then 'ok restored: blob == HEAD (63df3a1d892b)'. React's nested-anchor warning appears in the census run before the file family joined the set (1 hit) and in ablation leg 1 (2 hits), and in no unmutated run since (0). TYPE-CHECK at 27653b8, after 'pnpm --workspace-concurrency=2 --filter @object-ui/app-shell^... build' (BUILD_EXIT=0): 'pnpm --filter @object-ui/plugin-grid type-check' TC_GRID_EXIT=0 and 'pnpm --filter @object-ui/app-shell type-check' TC_SHELL_EXIT=0. Both scripts echoed 'tsc --noEmit && tsc -p tsconfig.test.json', and both tsconfig.test.json include src/**/*.test.tsx. LINT: eslint on the 4 touched files gives 0 errors; ObjectGrid.tsx has 207 warnings at HEAD and 207 at base (base file linted in place); the new tests have 0.",
