 "api_writes": "3 REST writes, each through the fleet-write relay (each relay write is one POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/dispatches executed as objectstack-fleet[bot]): (1) pr_create POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectui/pulls opened draft #11885, read back 7435 bytes sent and 7435 stored, identical; (2) label-write --assign os-support-ai POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectui/issues/11885/assignees, read back 'MATCHES the target', with no label writes; (3) this os-dev-report comment, POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectui/issues/11817/comments. git push is not counted (branch claude/issue-11817-invite-feedback).",
 "open_questions": [
  {
   "question": "Should #11885 keep 'Fixes #11817'? The toast's absence in the reporter's real browser is not measured. One candidate, not measured: sonner's 4s lifetime is shorter than a snapshot taken a turn after Confirm.",
   "options": [
    "A: keep Fixes. objectui's share is done; the copy and description halves go to an objectstack card.",
    "B: the seat edits the PR's first line to 'Part of #11817' until a booted-showcase reading of the toast exists."
   ],
   "recommendation": "A. The real chain renders the toast in the DOM (pinned, with a control), and nothing in objectui drops it. A live reading is a QA task, not an objectui change."
  }
 ],
 "out_of_scope_findings": [
  "class: a · reach: public door, Setup > Users > Invite User (and Approvals > Approve). The parameter dialog's subtitle reads 'Please provide the required information to continue.', because the action declares no description; objectui renders a declared one (pinned in ObjectView.inviteFeedback-11817.test.tsx with the ban_user shape). · evidence: objectstack 15ec50e5 packages/platform-objects/src/identity/sys-user.object.ts, sys-invitation.object.ts and sys-member.object.ts, each entry name: 'invite_user' with successMessage: 'Invitation sent' and no description key; packages/plugins/plugin-approvals/src/sys-approval-request.object.ts, entry name: 'approval_approve' with no description, while approval_reject beside it declares one. The generated translation bundles (packages/platform-objects/src/apps/translations/*.objects.generated.ts) would gain the matching description entries. · Seat: objectstack metadata, consumer ActionParamDialog via useConsoleActionRuntime paramCollectionHandler. · dedupe words: invite_user description · approval_approve description · param dialog subtitle metadata",
  "class: a · reach: public door, Setup > Users > Invite User > Confirm toasts 'Invitation sent', which names nobody, where the card expects a toast naming the invitee. Measured through the real chain in happy-dom, not live. · evidence: the runner fills ${result.*} from the answer (objectui#11344); the pin shows copy reading ${result.email} toasting 'Invitation sent to ada@example.com'. objectstack's invite_user entries (the same three files, successMessage: 'Invitation sent') and their generated bundle entries (_actions.invite_user.successMessage, which win over the authored literal) would both change. That the live invite-member answer carries email is read from auth-route-ledger.ts (source: better-auth), not measured. Same family as the finding above; one objectstack card suggested. · dedupe words: invite_user successMessage invitee · invitation sent toast email · result.email success copy",
  "carrier: 承接者:无 · noted, not filed (Acceptance notes of #11885): a rich-text value (markdown or html) whose content holds a link, drawn in a link column, still nests that link, because the content draws it; no shipped list is measured with such a primary or link column.",
  "carrier: 承接者:无 · noted, not filed: an image cell's '+N' button inside a link column is a button inside an anchor; React does not warn and no shipped list is measured.",
  "carrier: 承接者:无 · noted, not filed (read-only inference): useConsoleActionRuntime paramCollectionHandler's useCallback dependencies omit actionDescription and language, so a language switch could leave the dialog's description resolver stale; not measured."
 ],
